      "explanation": "<p>The structures of various molecules given in problem are discussed below -</p>\n<p>1. N<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub> It is the tautomeric mixture of following two structures -</p>\n<p> <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kz5qxcg2/6cadf172-fa85-47f5-b32e-576ecce28a1b/9e800220-8442-11ec-8bab-b14f78dd1244/file-1kz5qxcg3.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1kz5qxcg2/6cadf172-fa85-47f5-b32e-576ecce28a1b/9e800220-8442-11ec-8bab-b14f78dd1244/file-1kz5qxcg3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;max-height: 60vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2018 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - p-Block Elements Question 68 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1kz5qxcg2/6cadf172-fa85-47f5-b32e-576ecce28a1b/9e800220-8442-11ec-8bab-b14f78dd1244/file-1kz5qxcg3.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1kz5qxcg2/6cadf172-fa85-47f5-b32e-576ecce28a1b/9e800220-8442-11ec-8bab-b14f78dd1244/file-1kz5qxcg3.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kz5qxcg2/6cadf172-fa85-47f5-b32e-576ecce28a1b/9e800220-8442-11ec-8bab-b14f78dd1244/file-1kz5qxcg3.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1kz5qxcg2/6cadf172-fa85-47f5-b32e-576ecce28a1b/9e800220-8442-11ec-8bab-b14f78dd1244/file-1kz5qxcg3.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1kz5qxcg2/6cadf172-fa85-47f5-b32e-576ecce28a1b/9e800220-8442-11ec-8bab-b14f78dd1244/file-1kz5qxcg3.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1kz5qxcg2/6cadf172-fa85-47f5-b32e-576ecce28a1b/9e800220-8442-11ec-8bab-b14f78dd1244/file-1kz5qxcg3.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"> </p>\n<p>Conclusion 1 bridging oxo group is present in the compound.</p>\n<p>2. N<sub>2</sub>O<sub>5</sub> It has following structure.</p>\n<p> <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kz5qy5to/ec2307c1-7f84-42ed-a8cf-664e2f7ad56d/b531a3c0-8442-11ec-895a-013b39bd8d57/file-1kz5qy5tp.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1kz5qy5to/ec2307c1-7f84-42ed-a8cf-664e2f7ad56d/b531a3c0-8442-11ec-895a-013b39bd8d57/file-1kz5qy5tp.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;max-height: 60vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2018 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - p-Block Elements Question 68 English Explanation 2\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1kz5qy5to/ec2307c1-7f84-42ed-a8cf-664e2f7ad56d/b531a3c0-8442-11ec-895a-013b39bd8d57/file-1kz5qy5tp.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1kz5qy5to/ec2307c1-7f84-42ed-a8cf-664e2f7ad56d/b531a3c0-8442-11ec-895a-013b39bd8d57/file-1kz5qy5tp.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kz5qy5to/ec2307c1-7f84-42ed-a8cf-664e2f7ad56d/b531a3c0-8442-11ec-895a-013b39bd8d57/file-1kz5qy5tp.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1kz5qy5to/ec2307c1-7f84-42ed-a8cf-664e2f7ad56d/b531a3c0-8442-11ec-895a-013b39bd8d57/file-1kz5qy5tp.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1kz5qy5to/ec2307c1-7f84-42ed-a8cf-664e2f7ad56d/b531a3c0-8442-11ec-895a-013b39bd8d57/file-1kz5qy5tp.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1kz5qy5to/ec2307c1-7f84-42ed-a8cf-664e2f7ad56d/b531a3c0-8442-11ec-895a-013b39bd8d57/file-1kz5qy5tp.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>Conclusion 1 bridging oxo group is present in the compound.</p>\n<p>where, p<sub>i</sub> = initial pressure, p<sub>t</sub> = total pressure, y = number of gaseous products per mole of reactant</p>\n<p>3. P<sub>4</sub>O<sub>6</sub></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kz5qytt2/acf7b2c6-27b1-47e1-a8f